**Serious findings remain.** The per-candidate check can catch a false merge or a lost required question when that candidate is in G1, but it does not yet cover every relevant outcome or every evidence loss.

1. **Serious — the round-5 fix still misses directly filed evidence that both arms lose.** The plan checks direct evidence only when its destination changes against the control ([plan line 157](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:157)). If both runs drop the same required statement, there is no changed destination to inspect. Placement can drop an unfiled statement before matching ([placement.py line 53](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/placement.py:53); [extraction.py line 608](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/extraction.py:608)). The earlier audit recorded a case where the revenue page was present but a revenue statement was not filed there ([audit line 49](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/results.md:49)). That audit’s labels are not signed gold, but the example shows the gap. Required direct evidence needs an expected outcome independent of the control.

2. **Serious — the holdout does not specify how its existing questions come into being.** The plan says to run only extraction and placement for the new September week ([plan lines 133–134](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:133)). Placement needs the questions open at that article’s turn; matching and writing create those questions ([round.py lines 103–130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/views/round.py:103)). Without a defined starting ledger and a way to advance it, the holdout cannot establish the comparisons and evidence destinations G1 is meant to judge.

3. **Serious — the claimed closed set omits a real refusal outcome.** G1 says every ledger candidate is either its own question, the same as another, or a successor ([plan lines 107–115](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:107)). In the read-only [v38 ledger](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/english-v38-nvda-1w-2026-10-28/views.sqlite), item `gnews:6ab3379f10dfeb28924ebb57` has two candidates with the same question text; `n1` was refused because its object was outside the research universe. The product contract permits that refusal ([PRD 06 line 178](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/06-views.md:178)). “Same question” and “not worth opening” do not record why this candidate was correctly refused. Thus the round-4 structural rule covers the named successor cases, but is **not yet a complete closed set**.

4. **Serious — re-sampling placement makes the matching comparison ambiguous.** The plan says score changes come only from matching, while also re-sending placement because its list changes ([plan lines 144–147](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/plan.md:144)). Placement is a model call ([placement.py lines 59–70](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/placement.py:59)); a different placement answer can change evidence even with the same question list. The earlier audit explicitly says duplicate pages causing placement misses was **not proven** ([audit line 66](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-28-retention-audit/results.md:66)). The comparison therefore needs to distinguish matching’s effect from placement variation before attributing a score change.

The central source checks support several corrections already made. The guarantee/financing sentence is in both the [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:318) and the [collision prompt](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/src/hivemind/prompts/collision-v1.txt:1); its causing the ACP split remains unproven, as the plan now says. H1–H7 identify their principal changes as choices, and H7’s lean agrees with [D204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/DECISIONS.md:2609). The displayed census totals match the saved outputs, but verdict classes still depend on reason-text parsing ([census script line 25](/Users/lchingen/hivemind-extraction-quality-2026-10-28/docs/research/2026-10-30-question-identity/census/admission_census.py:25)). I did not independently verify every archived verdict, quote, estimate, or factual claim.

**Yes, serious findings remain.**
